#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "gitprotocol-http(5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:7
msgid "gitprotocol-http - Git HTTP-based protocols"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:13
msgid "<over-the-wire-protocol>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:22
msgid ""
"Git supports two HTTP based transfer protocols.  A \"dumb\" protocol which "
"requires only a standard HTTP server on the server end of the connection, "
"and a \"smart\" protocol which requires a Git aware CGI (or server module).  "
"This document describes both protocols."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:27
msgid ""
"As a design feature smart clients can automatically upgrade \"dumb\" "
"protocol URLs to smart URLs.  This permits all users to have the same "
"published URL, and the peers automatically select the most efficient "
"transport available to them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "URL Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:34
msgid ""
"URLs for Git repositories accessed by HTTP use the standard HTTP URL syntax "
"documented by RFC 1738, so they are of the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "  http://<host>:<port>/<path>?<searchpart>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:39
msgid ""
"Within this documentation the placeholder `$GIT_URL` will stand for the "
"http:// repository URL entered by the end-user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:44
msgid ""
"Servers SHOULD handle all requests to locations matching `$GIT_URL`, as both "
"the \"smart\" and \"dumb\" HTTP protocols used by Git operate by appending "
"additional path components onto the end of the user supplied `$GIT_URL` "
"string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:46
msgid "An example of a dumb client requesting a loose object:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $GIT_URL:     http://example.com:8080/git/repo.git\n"
"  URL request:  "
"http://example.com:8080/git/repo.git/objects/d0/49f6c27a2244e12041955e262a404c7faba355\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:51
msgid "An example of a smart request to a catch-all gateway:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $GIT_URL:     http://example.com/daemon.cgi?svc=git&q=\n"
"  URL request:  "
"http://example.com/daemon.cgi?svc=git&q=/info/refs&service=git-receive-pack\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:56
msgid "An example of a request to a submodule:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $GIT_URL:     http://example.com/git/repo.git/path/submodule.git\n"
"  URL request:  "
"http://example.com/git/repo.git/path/submodule.git/info/refs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:64
msgid ""
"Clients MUST strip a trailing `/`, if present, from the user supplied "
"`$GIT_URL` string to prevent empty path tokens (`//`) from appearing in any "
"URL sent to a server.  Compatible clients MUST expand `$GIT_URL/info/refs` "
"as `foo/info/refs` and not `foo//info/refs`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:72
msgid ""
"Standard HTTP authentication is used if authentication is required to access "
"a repository, and MAY be configured and enforced by the HTTP server "
"software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:76
msgid ""
"Because Git repositories are accessed by standard path components server "
"administrators MAY use directory based permissions within their HTTP server "
"to control repository access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:80
msgid ""
"Clients SHOULD support Basic authentication as described by RFC 2617.  "
"Servers SHOULD support Basic authentication by relying upon the HTTP server "
"placed in front of the Git server software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:83
msgid ""
"Servers SHOULD NOT require HTTP cookies for the purposes of authentication "
"or access control."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:86
msgid ""
"Clients and servers MAY support other common forms of HTTP based "
"authentication, such as Digest authentication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:93
msgid ""
"Clients and servers SHOULD support SSL, particularly to protect passwords "
"when relying on Basic HTTP authentication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session State"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:103
msgid ""
"The Git over HTTP protocol (much like HTTP itself) is stateless from the "
"perspective of the HTTP server side.  All state MUST be retained and managed "
"by the client process.  This permits simple round-robin load-balancing on "
"the server side, without needing to worry about state management."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:106
msgid ""
"Clients MUST NOT require state management on the server side in order to "
"function correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:111
msgid ""
"Servers MUST NOT require HTTP cookies in order to function correctly.  "
"Clients MAY store and forward HTTP cookies during request processing as "
"described by RFC 2616 (HTTP/1.1).  Servers SHOULD ignore any cookies sent by "
"a client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "General Request Processing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:119
msgid ""
"Except where noted, all standard HTTP behavior SHOULD be assumed by both "
"client and server.  This includes (but is not necessarily limited to):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:125
msgid ""
"If there is no repository at `$GIT_URL`, or the resource pointed to by a "
"location matching `$GIT_URL` does not exist, the server MUST NOT respond "
"with `200 OK` response.  A server SHOULD respond with `404 Not Found`, `410 "
"Gone`, or any other suitable HTTP status code which does not imply the "
"resource exists as requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:129
msgid ""
"If there is a repository at `$GIT_URL`, but access is not currently "
"permitted, the server MUST respond with the `403 Forbidden` HTTP status "
"code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:133
msgid ""
"Servers SHOULD support both HTTP 1.0 and HTTP 1.1.  Servers SHOULD support "
"chunked encoding for both request and response bodies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:137
msgid ""
"Clients SHOULD support both HTTP 1.0 and HTTP 1.1.  Clients SHOULD support "
"chunked encoding for both request and response bodies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:139
msgid "Servers MAY return ETag and/or Last-Modified headers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:142
msgid ""
"Clients MAY revalidate cached entities by including If-Modified-Since and/or "
"If-None-Match request headers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:146
msgid ""
"Servers MAY return `304 Not Modified` if the relevant headers appear in the "
"request and the entity has not changed.  Clients MUST treat `304 Not "
"Modified` identical to `200 OK` by reusing the cached entity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:150
msgid ""
"Clients MAY reuse a cached entity without revalidation if the Cache-Control "
"and/or Expires header permits caching.  Clients and servers MUST follow RFC "
"2616 for cache controls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "Discovering References"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:157
msgid ""
"All HTTP clients MUST begin either a fetch or a push exchange by discovering "
"the references available on the remote repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dumb Clients"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:164
msgid ""
"HTTP clients that only support the \"dumb\" protocol MUST discover "
"references by making a request for the special info/refs file of the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:167
msgid ""
"Dumb HTTP clients MUST make a `GET` request to `$GIT_URL/info/refs`, without "
"any search/query parameters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "   C: GET $GIT_URL/info/refs HTTP/1.0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:176
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:223
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   S: 200 OK\n"
"   S:\n"
"   S: 95dcfa3633004da0049d3d0fa03f80589cbcaf31\trefs/heads/maint\n"
"   S: d049f6c27a2244e12041955e262a404c7faba355\trefs/heads/master\n"
"   S: 2cb58b79488a98d2721cea644875a8dd0026b115\trefs/tags/v1.0\n"
"   S: a3c2e2402b99163d1d59756e5f207ae21cccba4c\trefs/tags/v1.0^{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:182
msgid ""
"The Content-Type of the returned info/refs entity SHOULD be `text/plain; "
"charset=utf-8`, but MAY be any content type.  Clients MUST NOT attempt to "
"validate the returned Content-Type.  Dumb servers MUST NOT return a return "
"type starting with `application/x-git-`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:185
msgid ""
"Cache-Control headers MAY be returned to disable caching of the returned "
"entity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:188
msgid ""
"When examining the response clients SHOULD only examine the HTTP status "
"code.  Valid responses are `200 OK`, or `304 Not Modified`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:193
msgid ""
"The returned content is a UNIX formatted text file describing each ref and "
"its known value.  The file SHOULD be sorted by name according to the C "
"locale ordering.  The file SHOULD NOT include the default ref named `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:196
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  info_refs   =  *( ref_record )\n"
"  ref_record  =  any_ref / peeled_ref\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:200
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  any_ref     =  obj-id HTAB refname LF\n"
"  peeled_ref  =  obj-id HTAB refname LF\n"
"\t\t obj-id HTAB refname \"^{}\" LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "Smart Clients"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:207
msgid ""
"HTTP clients that support the \"smart\" protocol (or both the \"smart\" and "
"\"dumb\" protocols) MUST discover references by making a parameterized "
"request for the info/refs file of the repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:212
msgid ""
"The request MUST contain exactly one query parameter, "
"`service=$servicename`, where `$servicename` MUST be the service name the "
"client wishes to contact to complete the operation.  The request MUST NOT "
"contain additional query parameters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "   C: GET $GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack HTTP/1.0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:216
msgid "dumb server reply:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:225
msgid "smart server reply:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:237
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   S: 200 OK\n"
"   S: Content-Type: application/x-git-upload-pack-advertisement\n"
"   S: Cache-Control: no-cache\n"
"   S:\n"
"   S: 001e# service=git-upload-pack\\n\n"
"   S: 0000\n"
"   S: 004895dcfa3633004da0049d3d0fa03f80589cbcaf31 "
"refs/heads/maint\\0multi_ack\\n\n"
"   S: 003fd049f6c27a2244e12041955e262a404c7faba355 refs/heads/master\\n\n"
"   S: 003c2cb58b79488a98d2721cea644875a8dd0026b115 refs/tags/v1.0\\n\n"
"   S: 003fa3c2e2402b99163d1d59756e5f207ae21cccba4c refs/tags/v1.0^{}\\n\n"
"   S: 0000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:241
msgid ""
"The client may send Extra Parameters (see linkgit:gitprotocol-pack[5]) as a "
"colon-separated string in the Git-Protocol HTTP header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:244
msgid "Uses the `--http-backend-info-refs` option to linkgit:git-upload-pack[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dumb Server Response"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:248
msgid "Dumb servers MUST respond with the dumb server reply format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:251
msgid ""
"See the prior section under dumb clients for a more detailed description of "
"the dumb server response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:252
#, no-wrap
msgid "Smart Server Response"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:257
msgid ""
"If the server does not recognize the requested service name, or the "
"requested service name has been disabled by the server administrator, the "
"server MUST respond with the `403 Forbidden` HTTP status code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:260
msgid ""
"Otherwise, smart servers MUST respond with the smart server reply format for "
"the requested service name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:263
msgid ""
"Cache-Control headers SHOULD be used to disable caching of the returned "
"entity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:270
msgid ""
"The Content-Type MUST be `application/x-$servicename-advertisement`.  "
"Clients SHOULD fall back to the dumb protocol if another content type is "
"returned.  When falling back to the dumb protocol clients SHOULD NOT make an "
"additional request to `$GIT_URL/info/refs`, but instead SHOULD use the "
"response already in hand.  Clients MUST NOT continue if they do not support "
"the dumb protocol."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:273
msgid ""
"Clients MUST validate the status code is either `200 OK` or `304 Not "
"Modified`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:277
msgid ""
"Clients MUST validate the first five bytes of the response entity matches "
"the regex `^[0-9a-f]{4}#`.  If this test fails, clients MUST NOT continue."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:280
msgid "Clients MUST parse the entire response as a sequence of pkt-line records."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:285
msgid ""
"Clients MUST verify the first pkt-line is `# service=$servicename`.  Servers "
"MUST set $servicename to be the request parameter value.  Servers SHOULD "
"include an LF at the end of this line.  Clients MUST ignore an LF at the end "
"of the line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:288
msgid ""
"Servers MUST terminate the response with the magic `0000` end pkt-line "
"marker."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:294
msgid ""
"The returned response is a pkt-line stream describing each ref and its known "
"value.  The stream SHOULD be sorted by name according to the C locale "
"ordering.  The stream SHOULD include the default ref named `HEAD` as the "
"first ref.  The stream MUST include capability declarations behind a NUL on "
"the first ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:297
msgid ""
"The returned response contains \"version 1\" if \"version=1\" was sent as an "
"Extra Parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:304
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  smart_reply     =  PKT-LINE(\"# service=$servicename\" LF)\n"
"\t\t     \"0000\"\n"
"\t\t     *1(\"version 1\")\n"
"\t\t     ref_list\n"
"\t\t     \"0000\"\n"
"  ref_list        =  empty_list / non_empty_list\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  empty_list      =  PKT-LINE(zero-id SP \"capabilities^{}\" NUL cap-list "
"LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  non_empty_list  =  PKT-LINE(obj-id SP name NUL cap_list LF)\n"
"\t\t     *ref_record\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:313
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  cap-list        =  capability *(SP capability)\n"
"  capability      =  1*(LC_ALPHA / DIGIT / \"-\" / \"_\")\n"
"  LC_ALPHA        =  %x61-7A\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:318
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ref_record      =  any_ref / peeled_ref\n"
"  any_ref         =  PKT-LINE(obj-id SP name LF)\n"
"  peeled_ref      =  PKT-LINE(obj-id SP name LF)\n"
"\t\t     PKT-LINE(obj-id SP name \"^{}\" LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:320
#, no-wrap
msgid "Smart Service git-upload-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:323
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:488
msgid "This service reads from the repository pointed to by `$GIT_URL`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:326
msgid ""
"Clients MUST first perform ref discovery with "
"`$GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:333
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   C: POST $GIT_URL/git-upload-pack HTTP/1.0\n"
"   C: Content-Type: application/x-git-upload-pack-request\n"
"   C:\n"
"   C: 0032want 0a53e9ddeaddad63ad106860237bbf53411d11a7\\n\n"
"   C: 0032have 441b40d833fdfa93eb2908e52742248faf0ee993\\n\n"
"   C: 0000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:340
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   S: 200 OK\n"
"   S: Content-Type: application/x-git-upload-pack-result\n"
"   S: Cache-Control: no-cache\n"
"   S:\n"
"   S: ....ACK %s, continue\n"
"   S: ....NAK\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:344
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:508
msgid ""
"Clients MUST NOT reuse or revalidate a cached response.  Servers MUST "
"include sufficient Cache-Control headers to prevent caching of the response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:346
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:510
msgid "Servers SHOULD support all capabilities defined here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:352
msgid ""
"Clients MUST send at least one \"want\" command in the request body.  "
"Clients MUST NOT reference an id in a \"want\" command which did not appear "
"in the response obtained through ref discovery unless the server advertises "
"capability `allow-tip-sha1-in-want` or `allow-reachable-sha1-in-want`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:357
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  compute_request   =  want_list\n"
"\t\t       have_list\n"
"\t\t       request_end\n"
"  request_end       =  \"0000\" / \"done\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:363
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  want_list         =  PKT-LINE(want SP cap_list LF)\n"
"\t\t       *(want_pkt)\n"
"  want_pkt          =  PKT-LINE(want LF)\n"
"  want              =  \"want\" SP id\n"
"  cap_list          =  capability *(SP capability)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "  have_list         =  *PKT-LINE(\"have\" SP id LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:367
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:529
msgid "TODO: Document this further."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Negotiation Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:372
msgid ""
"The computation to select the minimal pack proceeds as follows (C = client, "
"S = server):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:374
msgid "'init step:'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:376
msgid "C: Use ref discovery to obtain the advertised refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:378
msgid "C: Place any object seen into set `advertised`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:381
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"C: Build an empty set, `common`, to hold the objects that are later\n"
"   determined to be on both ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"C: Build a set, `want`, of the objects from `advertised` that the client\n"
"   wants to fetch, based on what it saw during ref discovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:389
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"C: Start a queue, `c_pending`, ordered by commit time (popping newest\n"
"   first).  Add all client refs.  When a commit is popped from\n"
"   the queue its parents SHOULD be automatically inserted back.\n"
"   Commits MUST only enter the queue once.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:391
msgid "'one compute step:'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:393
msgid "C: Send one `$GIT_URL/git-upload-pack` request:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   C: 0032want <want-#1>...............................\n"
"   C: 0032want <want-#2>...............................\n"
"   ....\n"
"   C: 0032have <common-#1>.............................\n"
"   C: 0032have <common-#2>.............................\n"
"   ....\n"
"   C: 0032have <have-#1>...............................\n"
"   C: 0032have <have-#2>...............................\n"
"   ....\n"
"   C: 0000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:411
msgid ""
"The stream is organized into \"commands\", with each command appearing by "
"itself in a pkt-line.  Within a command line, the text leading up to the "
"first space is the command name, and the remainder of the line to the first "
"LF is the value.  Command lines are terminated with an LF as the last byte "
"of the pkt-line value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:414
msgid ""
"Commands MUST appear in the following order, if they appear at all in the "
"request stream:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:416
msgid "\"want\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:417
msgid "\"have\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:419
msgid "The stream is terminated by a pkt-line flush (`0000`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:424
msgid ""
"A single \"want\" or \"have\" command MUST have one hex formatted object "
"name as its value.  Multiple object names MUST be sent by sending multiple "
"commands. Object names MUST be given using the object format negotiated "
"through the `object-format` capability (default SHA-1)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:427
msgid ""
"The `have` list is created by popping the first 32 commits from "
"`c_pending`.  Fewer can be supplied if `c_pending` empties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:432
msgid ""
"If the client has sent 256 \"have\" commits and has not yet received one of "
"those back from `s_common`, or the client has emptied `c_pending` it SHOULD "
"include a \"done\" command to let the server know it won't proceed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:434
#, no-wrap
msgid "   C: 0009done\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:436
msgid "S: Parse the git-upload-pack request:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:438
msgid "Verify all objects in `want` are directly reachable from refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:441
msgid ""
"The server MAY walk backwards through history or through the reflog to "
"permit slightly stale requests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:444
msgid ""
"If no \"want\" objects are received, send an error: TODO: Define error if no "
"\"want\" lines are requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:447
msgid ""
"If any \"want\" object is not reachable, send an error: TODO: Define error "
"if an invalid \"want\" is requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:449
msgid "Create an empty list, `s_common`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:451
msgid "If \"have\" was sent:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:453
msgid "Loop through the objects in the order supplied by the client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:457
msgid ""
"For each object, if the server has the object reachable from a ref, add it "
"to `s_common`.  If a commit is added to `s_common`, do not add any "
"ancestors, even if they also appear in `have`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:459
msgid "S: Send the git-upload-pack response:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:463
msgid ""
"If the server has found a closed set of objects to pack or the request ends "
"with \"done\", it replies with the pack.  TODO: Document the pack based "
"response"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:465
#, no-wrap
msgid "   S: PACK...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:470
msgid ""
"The returned stream is the side-band-64k protocol supported by the "
"git-upload-pack service, and the pack is embedded into stream 1.  Progress "
"messages from the server side MAY appear in stream 2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:473
msgid ""
"Here a \"closed set of objects\" is defined to have at least one path from "
"every \"want\" to at least one \"common\" object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:477
msgid ""
"If the server needs more information, it replies with a status continue "
"response: TODO: Document the non-pack response"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:479
msgid "C: Parse the upload-pack response:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:481
msgid "TODO: Document parsing response"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:483
msgid "'Do another compute step.'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:485
#, no-wrap
msgid "Smart Service git-receive-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:491
msgid ""
"Clients MUST first perform ref discovery with "
"`$GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-receive-pack`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:498
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   C: POST $GIT_URL/git-receive-pack HTTP/1.0\n"
"   C: Content-Type: application/x-git-receive-pack-request\n"
"   C:\n"
"   C: ....0a53e9ddeaddad63ad106860237bbf53411d11a7 "
"441b40d833fdfa93eb2908e52742248faf0ee993 refs/heads/maint\\0 report-status\n"
"   C: 0000\n"
"   C: PACK....\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:504
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   S: 200 OK\n"
"   S: Content-Type: application/x-git-receive-pack-result\n"
"   S: Cache-Control: no-cache\n"
"   S:\n"
"   S: ....\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:514
msgid ""
"Clients MUST send at least one command in the request body.  Within the "
"command portion of the request body clients SHOULD send the id obtained "
"through ref discovery as old_id."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:517
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  update_request  =  command_list\n"
"\t\t     \"PACK\" <binary-data>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:522
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  command_list    =  PKT-LINE(command NUL cap_list LF)\n"
"\t\t     *(command_pkt)\n"
"  command_pkt     =  PKT-LINE(command LF)\n"
"  cap_list        =  *(SP capability) SP\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitprotocol-http.txt:527
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  command         =  create / delete / update\n"
"  create          =  zero-id SP new_id SP name\n"
"  delete          =  old_id SP zero-id SP name\n"
"  update          =  old_id SP new_id SP name\n"
msgstr ""

